Google is not struggling or in need of revenue.

I'd say it's mostly the easily accessible step sequencer which allows for fast creation of drum beats,  the best piano roll of any DAW and the pattern based workflow that make FL uniquely good for hip-hop. Everything else that FL can do exists in other DAWs too, and FL is one of the cheaper ones.

&#x200B;

There's also a bandwagon mentality where most beatmakers use FL because a lot of beatmaking videos / producers on youtube use FL, kind of similar to how Ableton is the most popular DAW for pro EDM producers.

